# FESboard — custom electrical design rules
# Focus: protecting the ADS1298 (U2) analog electrode input path.
#
# Netclasses referenced here are defined in Board Setup > Net Classes.
#
# The clearance rules below are written with mutually exclusive netclass
# conditions, so at most one matches any given pair of objects and
# precedence between rules never comes into play. Keep that property if
# you add rules, or you will have to reason about evaluation order.

(version 1)


# =====================================================================
# 1. ELECTRODE INPUT ISOLATION
#    /IN1P../IN4N and /RLDOUT carry microvolt-level biopotentials at
#    PGA gains up to 12x. Any aggressor coupling here lands directly in
#    the 24-bit conversion, so buy distance wherever the layout allows.
# =====================================================================

(rule "ain_to_digital"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.5mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'AIN' && B.NetClass == 'DIG'"))

(rule "ain_to_usb"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.8mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'AIN' && B.NetClass == 'USB'"))

(rule "ain_to_power"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.6mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'AIN' && B.NetClass == 'PWR'"))

# The TPS62130 switch node is the loudest thing on this board:
# multi-amp edges at up to 2.25MHz on a large-dV/dt node.
(rule "ain_to_switch_node"
	(constraint clearance (min 2.0mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'AIN' && B.NetClass == 'SWNODE'"))

(rule "aref_to_switch_node"
	(constraint clearance (min 2.0mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'AREF' && B.NetClass == 'SWNODE'"))

# Local exception at U3 (TPS62130A): the switch node (SW, pin 3) sits next to
# PG (power-good, pin 4). PG is a slow DC-ish status output, not a sensitive
# node, so the 0.40mm SWNODE class clearance is overkill for this adjacent-pin
# pair and blocks the fanout. Relax SW<->PG only; SWNODE isolation from every
# other net is unchanged.
(rule "sw_to_pg_u3"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.2mm))
	(condition "(A.NetName == 'Net-(L1-Pad1)' && B.NetName == 'Net-(U3-PG)') || (A.NetName == 'Net-(U3-PG)' && B.NetName == 'Net-(L1-Pad1)')"))

# Same reasoning applied to the analog supply/reference decoupling.
(rule "aref_to_digital"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.4mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'AREF' && B.NetClass == 'DIG'"))


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# FINE-PITCH FANOUT AT U2 (ADS1298, 0.5mm-pitch TQFP-64)
#   The AIN/AREF class clearances are sized to isolate the electrode
#   path from aggressors (rules above). Between nets of the SAME class
#   -- e.g. two adjacent analog-input pins escaping the package, or the
#   VCAP/VREF decoupling nets -- that isolation is not needed and the
#   large clearance makes the pins impossible to route. Relax clearance
#   for same-class pairs only; the ain_to_* / aref_to_* rules still
#   enforce isolation from DIG / SWNODE / USB / PWR.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
(rule "ain_to_ain_fanout"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.15mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'AIN' && B.NetClass == 'AIN'"))

(rule "aref_to_aref_fanout"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.15mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'AREF' && B.NetClass == 'AREF'"))

# Let the analog nets neck down to the JLC manufacturing floor (0.15mm)
# at the fine-pitch pads, while still defaulting to the wider class width
# out in open copper.
(rule "ain_width_range"
	(constraint track_width (min 0.15mm) (opt 0.25mm) (max 0.4mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'AIN'"))

(rule "aref_width_range"
	(constraint track_width (min 0.15mm) (opt 0.3mm) (max 0.4mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'AREF'"))

# Fanout INSIDE the ADS1298 (U2). The 0.5mm-pitch TQFP-64 forces adjacent
# pins ~0.20mm apart, and an electrode-input trace must also squeeze past the
# neighbouring (often unconnected) pad to reach its pin. The AIN 0.40mm class
# clearance blocks both. Relax clearance to 0.15mm for pads AND tracks inside
# U2's courtyard -- but ONLY between benign nets. DIG / SWNODE / USB are
# excluded, so the ain_to_digital / ain_to_switch_node / ain_to_usb isolation
# still holds right at the pins (route those aggressors on the opposite layer).
(rule "ads_u2_fanout"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.15mm))
	(condition "A.intersectsCourtyard('U2') && B.intersectsCourtyard('U2') && A.NetClass != 'DIG' && A.NetClass != 'SWNODE' && A.NetClass != 'USB' && B.NetClass != 'DIG' && B.NetClass != 'SWNODE' && B.NetClass != 'USB'"))


# =====================================================================
# 2. DIFFERENTIAL SYMMETRY
#    CMRR depends on the two halves of each electrode pair seeing the
#    same interference. That means tight, symmetric coupling much more
#    than it means controlled impedance at these frequencies.
# =====================================================================

(rule "in_pair_uncoupled"
	(constraint diff_pair_uncoupled (max 5mm))
	(condition "A.inDiffPair('/IN*')"))

# Gap max is a CMRR rule, NOT a controlled-impedance rule. At EMG/ECG
# frequencies (DC-500Hz) the traces are electrically lumped -- a wavelength at
# 500Hz is ~300km against a 55mm trace -- so odd-mode impedance is meaningless
# and a tight 0.25mm gap buys nothing. What matters is that both halves of the
# pair traverse the SAME environment, so interference arrives common-mode and
# the PGA's ~115dB CMRR rejects it. A gap of 1-2mm does that perfectly well.
# Max is therefore set to catch genuinely DIVERGENT routing (P and N taking
# different paths across the board), not to enforce tight coupling.
(rule "in_pair_gap"
	(constraint diff_pair_gap (min 0.2mm) (opt 0.25mm) (max 2mm))
	(condition "A.inDiffPair('/IN*')"))


# =====================================================================
# 3. ANALOG KEEPOUT REGION
#    Draw a Rule Area covering U2's analog half plus the J2-J5 / BAV99
#    input network, and name it exactly "ANALOG_ZONE" (Rule Area
#    properties > Name). These rules then keep digital and switching
#    copper out of it on the routing layers.
#
#    Apply the area to F.Cu and B.Cu only -- NOT to In1.Cu. The whole
#    point of the 4-layer stackup is an unbroken In1.Cu ground plane
#    under the input network; excluding copper there would defeat it.
#    The rules below only disallow the DIG/SWNODE/USB netclasses, so
#    the In1.Cu plane (netclass PWR) is unaffected either way, but keep
#    the area off In1.Cu so later rule edits cannot slice the plane.
# =====================================================================

(rule "no_digital_in_analog_zone"
	(constraint disallow track via)
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'DIG' && A.insideArea('ANALOG_ZONE')"))

(rule "no_switching_in_analog_zone"
	(constraint disallow track via)
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'SWNODE' && A.insideArea('ANALOG_ZONE')"))

(rule "no_usb_in_analog_zone"
	(constraint disallow track via)
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'USB' && A.insideArea('ANALOG_ZONE')"))


# =====================================================================
# 4. CURRENT-CARRYING MINIMUMS
#    1oz outer copper, ~10-20 C rise.
# =====================================================================

# Power widths as ranges. The board is sense-only: max realistic load is
# ~1.5 A during USB-C fast charge, so 0.6mm (2.3 A capacity, 1oz outer,
# 10 C rise) is enough with 1.5x margin. Cap at 0.6mm so a wide pour is
# used instead of a fat trace once you need more copper than that.
# Min is the JLCPCB manufacturing floor for outer 1oz copper.
(rule "power_width_range"
	(constraint track_width (min 0.15mm) (opt 0.6mm) (max 0.6mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'PWR'"))

(rule "analog_supply_width_range"
	(constraint track_width (min 0.15mm) (opt 0.6mm) (max 0.6mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'APWR'"))

# SW node keeps a higher floor -- narrow SW radiates more than it saves
# space, and this net is the loudest thing on the board. If the TPS62130
# (U3) fanout physically can't accept 0.4mm, add a separate rule scoped
# to U3's courtyard only.
(rule "switch_node_width_range"
	(constraint track_width (min 0.4mm) (opt 0.6mm) (max 0.6mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'SWNODE'"))


